WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.193
<v Examiner>Three marks.

2
00:00:02.193 --> 00:00:06.956
<v Examiner>Compare an antiplatelet with an anticoagulant, giving an example of each,

3
00:00:06.956 --> 00:00:10.349
<v Examiner>and identify one nursing consideration for warfarin.

4
00:00:10.799 --> 00:00:14.201
An antiplatelet stops platelets sticking together.

5
00:00:14.201 --> 00:00:19.237
The example is aspirin, which in a low daily dose is given as prophylaxis,

6
00:00:19.237 --> 00:00:21.823
to prevent a heart attack or a stroke.

7
00:00:21.823 --> 00:00:26.994
Aspirin is also Joan's example of one drug in several classes: an analgesic,

8
00:00:26.994 --> 00:00:30.873
an antipyretic, an anti-inflammatory and an antiplatelet.

9
00:00:31.323 --> 00:00:35.596
An anticoagulant interferes with the clotting process itself.

10
00:00:35.596 --> 00:00:40.709
Warfarin is taken by mouth, and it's monitored with the I N R blood test;

11
00:00:40.709 --> 00:00:42.530
its antidote is vitamin K.

12
00:00:42.530 --> 00:00:48.134
Heparin is given by injection, subcutaneously, usually into the abdomen, or I V;

13
00:00:48.134 --> 00:00:51.286
it works fast, and its antidote is protamine.

14
00:00:51.286 --> 00:00:56.889
They relate because both stop clots forming, so both raise the risk of bleeding.

15
00:00:57.339 --> 00:01:00.315
A nursing consideration for warfarin, any one.

16
00:01:00.315 --> 00:01:06.137
Teach the signs of bleeding: bruising, bleeding gums, blood in the urine, or black stools.

17
00:01:06.137 --> 00:01:10.924
Check for interactions: aspirin together with warfarin increases bleeding,

18
00:01:10.924 --> 00:01:14.224
and the deck's example is warfarin with amiodarone.

19
00:01:14.224 --> 00:01:16.876
Alcohol and herbal remedies interact too.

20
00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:20.563
And warfarin is about ninety-nine per cent protein-bound,

21
00:01:20.563 --> 00:01:26.127
so very little free drug is around, and anything that displaces it changes its effect.

22
00:01:26.577 --> 00:01:30.817
Antiplatelet: stops platelets sticking, like low-dose aspirin.

23
00:01:30.817 --> 00:01:33.553
Anticoagulant: interferes with clotting.

24
00:01:33.553 --> 00:01:37.520
Warfarin by mouth, monitored by I N R, antidote vitamin K.

25
00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:40.324
Heparin by injection, antidote protamine.

26
00:01:40.324 --> 00:01:45.933
Both raise bleeding risk: teach bruising, bleeding gums, blood in urine or stools.

27
00:01:45.933 --> 00:01:49.147
Warfarin interacts with aspirin and amiodarone.
